{"causes": ["The strategic need for an alliance between the Swedish House of Bjälbo and the Danish monarchy prompted the marriage of Ingeborg to King Eric VI.", "The ongoing dynastic rivalries and territorial disputes between Sweden and Denmark necessitated diplomatic solutions through royal marriages.", "King Magnus Ladulås of Sweden sought to strengthen his kingdom's position by forging marital ties with neighboring powers like Denmark and Holstein."], "effects": ["Ingeborg's childless marriage to Eric VI directly contributed to a succession crisis in Denmark, leading to the ascension of Christopher II.", "Her life as Queen of Denmark temporarily stabilized relations between the Swedish and Danish crowns during a period of intense conflict.", "The absence of direct heirs from her marriage complicated the dynastic landscape of Scandinavia, influencing future claims and alliances."], "relationships": [{"sourceSlug": "eric-vi-of-denmark", "sourceName": "Eric VI of Denmark", "verb": "COLLABORATES_WITH", "targetSlug": "ingeborg-magnusdotter-of-sweden", "targetName": "Ingeborg Magnusdotter of Sweden", "context": "King Eric VI of Denmark married Ingeborg Magnusdotter in 1296 to secure a dynastic and political alliance with Sweden."}, {"sourceSlug": "magnus-ladulas", "sourceName": "Magnus Ladulås", "verb": "CAUSES", "targetSlug": "ingeborg-magnusdotter-of-sweden", "targetName": "Ingeborg Magnusdotter of Sweden", "context": "King Magnus Ladulås arranged Ingeborg's marriage to Eric VI of Denmark as a crucial strategic move for Swedish foreign policy."}, {"sourceSlug": "ingeborg-magnusdotter-of-sweden", "sourceName": "Ingeborg Magnusdotter of Sweden", "verb": "OCCURS_IN", "targetSlug": "denmark", "targetName": "Denmark", "context": "Ingeborg served as Queen of Denmark following her marriage to King Eric VI, residing primarily at the Danish court."}, {"sourceSlug": "succession-crisis-denmark-14th-century", "sourceName": "Danish Succession Crisis (14th Century)", "verb": "INFL